#: ../../advance/how-to.md:241
msgid "How to synthesize a long spectra"
msgstr ""

#: ../../advance/how-to.md:243
msgid ""
"The synthesis of long spectra, i.e., a spectra covering a wide wavelength"
" range (>100AA) or a spectra divided into many chunks but still cover a "
"wide wavelength range, would be a bit tricky."
msgstr ""

#: ../../advance/how-to.md:245
msgid ""
"The deafult synthesis mode of PySME takes all the lines in the `linelist`"
" into account to synthesize the spectra, thus the synthesis takes a long "
"time. To make it even worse, the synthesis is repeated for each segment, "
"thus if we have 10 segment covering from 3000-9000AA, all the lines "
"(including those in ~9000AA) will be used for the first segment "
"(3000-3600AA), and the total time cost is 10 times longer than just using"
" one segment to cover the whole range."
msgstr ""

#: ../../advance/how-to.md:248
msgid ""
"This situation can be improved by using the central depth and line range "
"parameters to select the relevant lines for each segment, by simply "
"adding `linelist_mode='dynamic'` in `synthesize_spectrum`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../advance/how-to.md:262
msgid ""
"`linelist_mode='auto'` is still accepted as a deprecated compatibility "
"alias and maps to `linelist_mode='dynamic'`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../advance/how-to.md:265
msgid ""
"The detailed explanaiton of what `linelist_mode='dynamic'` triggers is as"
" follow:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../advance/how-to.md:267
msgid ""
"If the `sme.linelist.cdr_paras` is None (means `update_cdr` hasn't run "
"for it), or either the Teff, logg, monh and vmic (optional) in "
"`sme.linelist.cdr_paras` differ from the input parameters by 250K, 0.5, "
"0.5 or 1 (you can change these parameter in "
"`sme.linelist.cdr_paras_thres` as a dictionary), then run `update_cdr` "
"under current input stellar parameters."
msgstr ""

#: ../../advance/how-to.md:268
msgid "Find the beginning and ending wavelength of each segment, wbeg and wend."
msgstr ""

#: ../../advance/how-to.md:269
msgid "For each segment, only input the lines with:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../advance/how-to.md:270
msgid "`central_depth` > sme.cdr_depth_thres (default 0), and"
msgstr ""

#: ../../advance/how-to.md:271
msgid "`line_range_s` <= wend + del_wav + line_margin, and"
msgstr ""

#: ../../advance/how-to.md:272
msgid "`line_range_e` >= wbeg - del_wav - line_margin"
msgstr ""

#: ../../advance/how-to.md:273
msgid "Finish the synthesis."
msgstr ""

#: ../../advance/how-to.md:275
msgid ""
"Here del_wav is defined as sqrt(sme.vmic^2 + sme.vmac^2 + "
"sme.vsini^2)/c*lambda + lambda/sme.ipres, and line_margin is set to 2AA "
"(just for adding some margin). NLTE calculation is also availalbe in this"
" mode, by setting `sme.nlte.set_nlte`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../advance/how-to.md:278
msgid ""
"Note that the input line list will not change - only the lines being "
"input to each segment synthesis will differ."
msgstr ""

#: ../../advance/how-to.md:280
msgid ""
"Removing the `linelist_mode` variable or changing it to `all` falls back "
"to the default way to perform synthesis, described in the beginning of "
"this section."
msgstr ""

